        {
          "type": "Body",
          "props": {
            "text": "The purpose of this SOP is to define the process for planning, developing, executing, maintaining, and archiving the Asset Level Safety Assessment Plan (ALSAP) for use in asset-level safety monitoring during clinical development.",
            "kicker": "Why this"
          },
          "meta": {
            "element_id": "ele_sop_ast29080_purpose__activate",
            "composed_from": "atom_sop_ast29080_purpose",
            "text_primitive": "tp_callout",
            "style_ref": "brand.prior"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "Body",
          "props": {
            "text": "The purpose of this SOP is to define the process for planning, developing, executing, maintaining, and archiving the Asset Level Safety Assessment Plan (ALSAP) for use in asset-level safety monitoring during clinical development.",
            "kicker": "Purpose"
          },
          "meta": {
            "element_id": "ele_sop_ast29080_purpose",
            "composed_from": "atom_sop_ast29080_purpose",
            "text_primitive": "tp_purpose",
            "style_ref": "brand.purpose"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "Body",
          "props": {
            "text": "This SOP applies to all Astellas and non-Astellas employees responsible for supporting ALSAP throughout its lifecycle. The in-scope organizations are listed below.",
            "kicker": "Present"
          },
          "meta": {
            "element_id": "ele_sop_ast29080_scope",
            "composed_from": "atom_sop_ast29080_scope",
            "text_primitive": "tp_body",
            "style_ref": "brand.instructional"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "Body",
          "props": {
            "text": "The ALSAP is the central cross-functional framework for ongoing identification, evaluation, and communication of emerging safety risks at the asset level. It operationalizes the existing safety governance documents listed below, integrating them into an actionable, data-driven plan for aggregate monitoring across all relevant clinical trials. Only one ALSAP exists per asset. It must meet ALCOA+ standards and is reviewed annually by the SMT, with ad hoc updates triggered by emerging signals, regulatory changes, milestones, data-quality concerns, or external safety events.",
            "kicker": "Present"
          },
          "meta": {
            "element_id": "ele_sop_ast29080_general",
            "composed_from": "atom_sop_ast29080_general",
            "text_primitive": "tp_body",
            "style_ref": "brand.instructional"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
